    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be implemented on latest `main`. The most serious changed compared to the previous behavior is the name of the 'mini.starter' buffer: when opening Neovim it was `Starter`  (which showed rather nicely in the statusline and is more or less user-friendly) and now it is `ministarter://1/welcome` (which looks somewhat intimidating, but that is the price for consistency).\n\nOn the upside, the `:buffers!` is now much more explicit about its permanent hidden buffers. They are mostly there for performance reasons (no need to create-delete-create-delete-etc buffer for the same purpose, just one buffer is reused) and now less confusing than all `[Scratch]` and `[No name]` entries that were there previously.",
            "created_at": "2025-03-27T11:40:46Z",
